<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Runtime reconfiguration of the talker app, driven by INET's ScenarioManager
    (see *.scenarioManager.script in omnetpp_uplink.ini,
    [Config UplinkRuntimeParams]).

    That config cuts tsnDeviceB down to a single UdpBasicApp sending a fixed
    100B payload every 1ms, so the run has exactly one thing to watch and the
    only variable is the period.

    <set-param> assigns a new value to a module parameter mid-run. It only has
    a visible effect for parameters the owning module re-reads after
    initialize(), which is the case here: UdpBasicApp.cc:156 reads
    par("sendInterval") every time it schedules the next send, so the new rate
    takes effect from the *next* packet on (the send already scheduled at t=2s
    still fires at the old spacing).

    Parameters that are cached into a C++ member during initialize() will NOT
    react to <set-param>: notably every knob of Simu5G's channel model
    (LteRealisticChannelModel.cc:47-92). See ue0_walkaway.xml for the way to
    change radio conditions at runtime.
-->
<scenario>
    <at t="2s">
        <!-- Periodic traffic: 1ms -> 100ms, i.e. 1000pps down to 10pps. -->
        <set-param module="tsnDeviceB.app[0]" par="sendInterval" value="100ms"/>
    </at>
</scenario>
